        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The pros of tankless are endless hot water, a 20-year life, lower gas bills and the floor space back. The cons are a flow-rate ceiling, the cold-water sandwich, a minimum flow to fire, annual descaling, no hot water in a blackout and an installed price well above a tank.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Tankless is worth it when running out of hot water is your real problem, you have the gas supply to feed it, and you will stay long enough to collect on its lifespan. If that is you, size it for winter and choose from our tested picks. If your home is all-electric, look hard at a heat pump water heater first.
          </p>
